{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumH6fTFsx2THwCckWmh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It sends the standard MCP `initialize` JSON-RPC request, which carries the client's `protocolVersion`, its `capabilities`, and `clientInfo` (name and version). The Agents SDK's MCP client wraps the official `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` `Client`, so it follows the normal handshake. Once the server replies, the client sends a `notifications/initialized` notification, and only then lists tools, prompts and resources.\n\nWith the Streamable HTTP transport, `initialize` goes out as the first HTTP POST. With the legacy SSE transport, the first thing is a GET that opens the event stream, and `initialize` is POSTed to the endpoint the server announces. If the server requires OAuth, an unauthenticated request can get a 401 first, which triggers the auth flow before the handshake completes.\n\nI'm answering from my knowledge of the protocol and SDK, not from the current Agents source, so the transport-fallback details may differ in the latest version."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2251,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2251},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c566db02-eea3-4eab-ae7d-5c58ba3199e4","uuid":"38448fc8-7528-4e38-b6d6-aa536f52df3b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:47:02.484Z","request_id":"req_011CfumH6R5UfL64sLVrfdbe"}
